# Graphualize — Supabase Auth
#
# Copy to `.env.local` and fill in. `.env.local` is gitignored.
#
# BOTH of these values are PUBLISHABLE and are meant to ship to the browser.
# The anon key is safe in a client bundle: it grants only what row-level
# security allows. Nothing secret belongs in this file or any VITE_ variable —
# Vite inlines every VITE_* value into the JavaScript it serves.
#
# Specifically, these NEVER go here:
#   - the Google OAuth client secret  -> Supabase dashboard only
#   - the Supabase service-role key   -> server-side only, never in a browser
#   - a Supabase personal access token -> your shell, for CLI/Management API use
#
# Leave both blank and Graphualize runs exactly as it always has, anonymously,
# with no account UI. Authentication is additive.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
